BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Build a Library
DTSTART:20250516T203000Z
DTEND:20250516T222000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T203000Z
UID:9lwfydGOfO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nWhen two local women set out to 
 decolonize Nairobi’s formerly whites-only McMillan Memorial Library and 
 turn it into a multicultural hub\, they must contend with their country’
 s history and a complicated web of bureaucracy over eight very long but re
 warding years. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/how-to-build
 -a-library\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Wed 21 M
 ay\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blue Road: The Edna O'Brien Story
DTSTART:20250516T230000Z
DTEND:20250517T005000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T230000Z
UID:U7CdAtZx3f
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nThe controversial and boldly fem
 inist Irish author Edna O’Brien (“The Country Girls”) shares journal
  entries and provocative insight into her trailblazing career in a series 
 of late-in-life interviews in this Palm Springs International Film Festiva
 l award winner. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/blue-road-t
 he-edna-obrien-story\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1
  (Tue 20 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Invention
DTSTART:20250517T013000Z
DTEND:20250517T025500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T013000Z
UID:8nGOMXbXwZ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 72 mins (1h12m)\n\nCallie Hernandez (The Endless) co
 -writes and stars in this inventive\, autofictional indie that evokes the 
 tone of a Haruki Murakami detective story\, as a daughter investigates her
  estranged late father’s experimental health marketing schemes. Director
  Courtney Stephens scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/festival/invention\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House
  3 (Sat 17 May\, 12:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Nature of Invisible Things
DTSTART:20250517T040000Z
DTEND:20250517T054000Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T040000Z
UID:PyMFo8kFHF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nGloria and Sofia\, two 10-year-ol
 d girls\, meet during the summer holidays while spending the days in a hos
 pital. Gloria is accompanying her nurse mother and Sofia is visiting her g
 randmother with Alzheimer’s. Their playful and delicate bond will help t
 hem navigate the fragility of life. Director Rafaela Camelo scheduled to a
 ttend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-nature-of-invisi
 ble-things\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Sat 17 M
 ay\, 3:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mongrels
DTSTART:20250517T174500Z
DTEND:20250517T194500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T174500Z
UID:k1l4Ml5hKs
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nIn this triptych of stories\, a 
 Korean father and his two children move to the Canadian prairies to help a
  town deal with its feral dog population\, all while making a new life in 
 a strange land and navigating the grief of an absent mother. Director Jero
 me Yoo scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/mongrels\n\nA
 lso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Fri 16 May\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chain Reactions
DTSTART:20250517T203000Z
DTEND:20250517T222500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T203000Z
UID:NjjQTSHNHs
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nFilm essayist and SIFF alum Alex
 andre O. Philippe (78/52\, Lynch/Oz) calls upon five horror luminaries—S
 tephen King and Takashi Miike among them—to discuss the impact 1974’s 
 seminal The Texas Chain Saw Massacre had upon their lives and careers. Di
 rector Alexandre Philippe scheduled to attend. Swap your leather face for 
 your thinking cap at the May 16 screening\, where BoneBat Comedy of Horror
 s Film Fest will be giving away goodies via trivia! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps
 ://www.siff.net/festival/chain-reactions\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF C
 inema Uptown House 2 (Fri 16 May\, 9:00 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:F*cktoys
DTSTART:20250517T231500Z
DTEND:20250518T011500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T231500Z
UID:INJl9fQN9R
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 107 mins (1h47m)\n\nAnnapurna Sriram writes\, direct
 s\, and stars in this campy\, vividly pastel-colored romp about a woman wh
 o embarks upon a sex worker odyssey through Trashtown with her nonbinary f
 riend to break a terrible curse that has befallen her. SXSW Special Jury P
 rize winner. Director Annapurna Sriram scheduled to attend. Keep your biza
 rre odyssey through queer cinema going with a chance to win tickets to the
  Queer & Trans Film Festival at the screening on May 16. Sponsored by:\n\n
 https://www.siff.net/festival/fucktoys\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cin
 ema Uptown House 1 (Fri 16 May\, 9:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
