BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jean Cocteau
DTSTART:20250520T020000Z
DTEND:20250520T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T020000Z
UID:dcW3XBPaPX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nLisa Immordino Vreeland (SIFF 202
 1’s Truman & Tennessee: An Intimate Conversation) constructs an astonish
 ing portrait of polymath Jean Cocteau—filmmaker\, playwright\, poet—to
 ld in his own words using his journals\, letters\, and artistic works. Pro
 ducer/Editor John Northrup scheduled to attend. Come early to the May 20 s
 creening to find out about ACT Contemporary Theatre's upcoming production 
 of "Twelfth Night" and get the chance to win a pair of tickets to the play
 !  Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/jean-cocteau\n\nAlso pla
 ying at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Tue 20 May\, 3:00 PM)\n\nFilm 
 is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
